King James Version (KJV) — Attribution & Licensing
===================================================

The King James Version of the Holy Bible was first published in 1611
under the authority of King James I of England. The text is in the
public domain worldwide.

Source
------

The kjv.pdf file in this directory is a PDF rendering of the complete
KJV text (66 books, 1,189 chapters, 31,102 verses). The underlying
scripture text is public domain; the PDF layout/typesetting is provided
as a convenience for parsing.

Use
---

soap-journal bundles this text so the application ships with two
translations out of the box (BSB and KJV), enabling the side-by-side
translation comparison feature without any additional setup. The parser
at backend/soap_journal/parsers/kjv.py converts this source into the
canonical JSON schema defined in backend/soap_journal/parsers/schema.py;
the loader at backend/soap_journal/cli/load_translation.py ingests that
canonical JSON into the application database.
